.TH USERS-PRO 8 "2026-08-08" "users-pro 2.2.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
users-pro \- local account lifecycle management with a terminal interface
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B users-pro
.RI [ command ]
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B users-pro tui
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B users-pro
manages local user accounts on Ubuntu 26.04 LTS: creation, deletion, editing,
password and aging policy, group membership, per-user SSH
.B PasswordAuthentication
and
.BR authorized_keys ,
and optional managed sudoers drop-ins.
.PP
Run without arguments it launches a full-screen interface. Every operation is
also available as a scriptable subcommand.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B tui
Launch the interactive interface. Without root it is read-only.
.TP
.B add
Create an account.
.TP
.B delete
Delete an account and its artifacts.
.TP
.B info
Detailed report for one account.
.TP
.B list
List accounts.
.TP
.B edit
Modify an existing account.
.TP
.B disable
Lock, expire and set nologin in one step.
.TP
.B enable
Reverse
.BR disable .
.TP
.B keys
Manage SSH authorized_keys.
.TP
.B audit
Show recent audit log entries.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Report intended actions without applying them.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Assume yes for all confirmations.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress informational output.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Emit debug output.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Machine-readable output for
.B info
and
.BR list .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable ANSI colour.
.TP
.BI \-\-audit\-log " PATH"
Override the audit log path.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 64
Usage error.
.TP
.B 65
Invalid data.
.TP
.B 67
No such user.
.TP
.B 69
Missing dependency.
.TP
.B 70
Internal failure.
.TP
.B 77
Permission denied.
.TP
.B 78
Configuration error.
.TP
.B 79
Conflict.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/log/users-pro.log
Audit trail of every mutation, mode 0640.
.TP
.I /etc/ssh/sshd_config.d/99-users-pro-USER.conf
Managed per-user SSH drop-in.
.TP
.I /etc/sudoers.d/90-users-pro-USER
Managed NOPASSWD sudoers entry.
.TP
.I /run/lock/users-pro.lock
Advisory lock against concurrent runs.
.SH SECURITY
Passwords are passed to
.BR chpasswd (8)
through the shell's
.B printf
builtin and never appear in process arguments. Home directory archives are
created mode 0600. SSH configuration changes are validated with
.B sshd -t
and rolled back if rejected.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
users-pro tui
users-pro add -u deploy --groups docker --generate-password
users-pro edit -u deploy --max-days 90 --add-groups www-data
users-pro list --json | jq '.[] | select(.state=="LOCKED")'
users-pro --dry-run delete -u olduser --backup-home /var/backups/old.tar.gz
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR useradd (8),
.BR usermod (8),
.BR userdel (8),
.BR chage (1),
.BR sshd_config (5),
.BR sudoers (5)
